            {
                "entry_id": "37c50de5-dbf2-3e99-aa53-47579173d33a",
                "word": "uitdoving",
                "pos": "noun",
                "lang_code": "nl",
                "forms": [
                    {
                        "form_id": "31abd78e-cd46-4c46-ad26-7eb6b5e33da6",
                        "entry_id": "37c50de5-dbf2-3e99-aa53-47579173d33a",
                        "tags": [
                            "plural"
                        ],
                        "form": "uitdovingen"
                    }
                ],
                "senses": [
                    {
                        "sense_id": "67d51429-7b52-387d-b9e5-5111ee06b8a3",
                        "entry_id": "37c50de5-dbf2-3e99-aa53-47579173d33a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "het uitgaan van een vuur"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "4b5d7a7d-2932-4efb-85a6-a3890d92badd",
                                "sense_id": "67d51429-7b52-387d-b9e5-5111ee06b8a3",
                                "text": "Of de kosmische uitdoving in hetzelfde tempo zal doorgaan, of zal vertragen of versnellen, is onduidelijk. Volgens de Leidse astronoom Benne Holwerda, een van de Nederlanders die bij de grote survey betrokken zijn, is dat afhankelijk van de hoeveelheid gas die sterrenstelsels ‘in reserve’ hebben of nog weten aan te trekken."
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "82d74003-e386-3ed6-a126-3999beee631d",
                        "entry_id": "37c50de5-dbf2-3e99-aa53-47579173d33a",
                        "glosses": [
                            "het stoppen, minder worden, of afschaffen van iets"
                        ],
                        "tags": [],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "765b7843-0040-4017-972c-64673c33cf7e",
                                "sense_id": "82d74003-e386-3ed6-a126-3999beee631d",
                                "text": "In 2016 is het vuur van de passie voor voetbal geconfronteerd met verschijnselen van uitdoving. Althans, de hype heeft zich verplaatst naar het F1-circuit met Max Verstappen en naar dartcafés. Een aantal clubs zit in financiële nood waardoor de geeuwhonger van buitenlandse investeerders niet meer tegen te houden is. De uitverkoop van de kroonjuwelen is begonnen."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "10b65365-5b35-45cc-b8fd-a97ac161bb76",
                                "sense_id": "82d74003-e386-3ed6-a126-3999beee631d",
                                "text": "‘Als je de startnota van de premier over de arbeidsdeal leest, dan komt het erop neer dat de federale regering de regio’s vertelt wat ze moeten doen. Dat toont het gebrek aan politieke moed: men kijkt vooral naar elkaar. Terwijl de federale overheid heel veel zelf kan doen. Waarom staat er in die nota niets over de versnelde uitdoving van het SWT-stelsel?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "9ec1b19e-458c-49a4-95be-cc07308da73b",
                                "sense_id": "82d74003-e386-3ed6-a126-3999beee631d",
                                "text": "Toepassing van een ‘frequentiekam’ kan uitdoving van het optische signaal in glasvezels sterk verminderen."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
                "translations": [
                    {
                        "translation_id": "2df13d13-7915-4293-978f-f5ca84c72d81",
                        "source_entry_id": "37c50de5-dbf2-3e99-aa53-47579173d33a",
                        "source_sense_id": "67d51429-7b52-387d-b9e5-5111ee06b8a3",
                        "target_lang_word": "extinction",
                        "target_lang_code": "en",
                        "target_sense_ids": [],
                        "cross_references": [
                            {
                                "target_word": "extinction",
                                "target_lang_code": "en",
                                "target_senses": [
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "48bf5c95-1ea3-36d6-95cf-5bb1c44cbe91",
                                        "entry_id": "d628bd53-9d45-3ca6-8c51-6639a3ea8beb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The action of making or becoming extinct; annihilation."
                                        ],
                                        "tags": [
                                            "countable",
                                            "uncountable"
                                        ],
                                        "examples": [
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "58cf3d60-6ba4-4ce5-aa25-5055d31413f9",
                                                "sense_id": "48bf5c95-1ea3-36d6-95cf-5bb1c44cbe91",
                                                "text": "Thirteen long centuries have elapsed since the extinction of the last Zoroastrian Empire[…]"
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "0ffdad48-256e-4ad6-af0d-9f21c769418c",
                                                "sense_id": "48bf5c95-1ea3-36d6-95cf-5bb1c44cbe91",
                                                "text": "Their lives were short; all were condemned by the early 1930s, presumably because, like most classes of G.S.W.R. engines, their small numbers invited extinction under any comprehensive programme of standardisation."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "2267dc23-4c3a-4f7f-9f35-adf29a71c261",
                                                "sense_id": "48bf5c95-1ea3-36d6-95cf-5bb1c44cbe91",
                                                "text": "The extinction of a species once so numerous seemed incredible."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "f593e878-e8a8-4d5a-8f3f-4756201316ba",
                                                "sense_id": "48bf5c95-1ea3-36d6-95cf-5bb1c44cbe91",
                                                "text": "Dr. Manuel: You're wasting your time. The age of humanity is over. Our extinction is inevitable."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "a3e4deae-4dbc-4838-8ac1-9866341c690c",
                                                "sense_id": "48bf5c95-1ea3-36d6-95cf-5bb1c44cbe91",
                                                "text": "Phoenix and Lubbock are both caught in severe drought, and it is going to get much worse. We may see many such [dust] storms in the decades ahead, along with species extinctions, radical disturbance of ecosystems, and intensified social conflict over land and water. Welcome to the Anthropocene, the epoch when humans have become a major geological and climatic force."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "21d87b57-91af-443d-af79-2ec421e0a79d",
                                                "sense_id": "48bf5c95-1ea3-36d6-95cf-5bb1c44cbe91",
                                                "text": "On the East and West Coast Main Lines in the 1950s/60s, for example, we saw the extinction of intermediate stations in order to create the same sort of accelerations that IRP is now promising. Back then, the priority was faster main line services, with wayside/intermediate stations paying the ultimate price."
                                            },
                                            {
                                                "example_id": "13bd366b-fbfa-4515-9991-4dc58a4f4ba0",
                                                "sense_id": "48bf5c95-1ea3-36d6-95cf-5bb1c44cbe91",
                                                "text": "In Perthshire, the Aberdeenshire catchments of Deeside and Donside, in Moray and Nairnshire to the north-east, the populations are in low single figures, putting them on the brink of local extinction."
                                            }
                                        ]
                                    },
                                    {
                                        "sense_id": "bce03888-7e95-3aa2-b301-6520e9c0fe28",
                                        "entry_id": "d628bd53-9d45-3ca6-8c51-6639a3ea8beb",
                                        "glosses": [
                                            "The absorption or scattering of electromagnetic radiation emitted by astronomical objects by intervening dust and gas before it reaches the observer."
                                        ],
